    "topic": "Laws of Motion",
    "subtopic": "Newton's Laws & Friction",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "questionText": "Two blocks of masses \ud835\udc401 and \ud835\udc402 are connected with a string which passes over a smooth pulley. The mass \ud835\udc401 is placed on a rough incline plane as shown in the figure. The coefficient of friction between the block and the inclined plane is\ud835\udf07. What should be the minimum mass \ud835\udc402 so that the block \ud835\udc401 slides upwards?",
